+---
+id: task-005-booking-cancellation-cancel-bookingid-at
+type: task
+title: "Booking cancellation: cancel(bookingId, at)"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Booking cancellation: cancel(bookingId, at)
+
+Plans change, and customers ask us to cancel their bookings. The rental service needs a way to cancel a booking.
+
+## Requested behaviour
+
+Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental service. It cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns
+`{ bookingId, refund }`, where `refund` is the amount given back to the customer, in euro cents.
+
+A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, so its item is free again for overlapping periods. A booking can
+only be cancelled once.
+
+## School rules
+
+Cancellation policy (task-001, school rule 5): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start gets no
+refund; otherwise the full amount of the booking is refunded.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+- `at` is a UTC ISO-8601 instant ending in `Z`, e.g. `2026-07-01T10:00:00Z`, with optional seconds and fractional
+  seconds. Other strings and impossible dates throw.
+- `refund` is the booking's `total` (the long-stay discounted total when it applies) when the time from `at` to the
+  booking's `start` is 24 hours or more, and `0` when it is less than 24 hours. Exactly 24 hours before gets the full
+  refund.
+- A cancellation at or after `start` is allowed: it is less than 24 hours before the start, so `refund` is `0`, and it
+  frees the item.
+- `bookingId` must be the id returned by `book`. An unknown id throws. A second cancellation of the same booking throws.
+- The booking stays in the service as cancelled, so booking ids remain sequential and deterministic.
+- Cancelling does not change `availability` results for other bookings.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Cancelling 2 or more days before the start returns the full booked total as `refund`.
+- Cancelling less than 24 hours before the start returns `refund` 0.
+- Cancelling exactly 24 hours before the start returns the full total.
+- A long-stay booking refunds its discounted total.
+- After cancellation the item is free for an overlapping period, both by `book` and by `availability`.
+- An unknown booking id throws; cancelling the same booking twice throws.
+- An invalid `at` throws.
+- Tests are deterministic and in-process, with no external services.
+- The README describes `cancel` and its refund policy, replacing "Cancellations are not implemented yet."
